            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>This Week's Observations: Three Changes Impacting Cold Launches</h2>
<p>This week, while assisting several TikTok Shop cold launch projects, we noticed several signals worth attention.</p>
<p><strong>First, promotional period traffic windows are fluctuating.</strong> Some categories' new product exposure support is less stable than last month, meaning relying solely on organic platform traffic for launches is becoming harder.</p>
<p><strong>Second, user tolerance for homogenized content has dropped significantly.</strong> Content that doesn't capture attention within the first 3 seconds shows about 15-20% higher bounce rates compared to last month.</p>
<p><strong>Third, requirements for content originality are increasing.</strong> Mass repurposed or simple remade content is seeing noticeable drops in recommended reach.</p>
<p>These changes directly impact cold launch phases: the previous approach of "one creative asset to rule them all" is increasingly difficult to execute. The richness and iteration speed of your creative pool have become key variables.</p>
<hr />
<h2>This Week's Case: A Tool App's 48-Hour Creative Testing Method</h2>
<p>We tracked a tool app's TikTok Shop cold launch process this week. Their approach is worth referencing:</p>
<p><strong>Day 1 (Morning):</strong> Prepared 6 test creatives from different angles, covering product display, use cases, and pain point solutions. Each creative budget was controlled at $20-30, with TikTok + Facebook Reels as the test platforms.</p>
<p><strong>Day 1 (Afternoon) - Day 2 Morning:</strong> Monitored data, completing the first round of data collection within 2 hours. Focused on CTR and completion rate metrics.</p>
<p><strong>Day 2 Afternoon:</strong> Eliminated the bottom 2 performing creatives, concentrating budget on the top 3 performers. Quickly filmed 2 new angle creatives to maintain test pool activity.</p>
<p><strong>Results:</strong> Found 2 creatives with CTR exceeding 3% within 48 hours, with cost per acquisition approximately 22% lower than industry average.</p>
<p>The insight from this case: <strong>The core of the cold launch phase is not "selecting the best creative," but "quickly filtering out a creative combination."</strong></p>
<hr />
<h2>This Week's Impact: Why Creative Pool Is Now Essential</h2>
<p>Over the past six months, many overseas teams' creative strategy was "run one first, replenish if it works." But this week's observations show this strategy's risks are rising:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Platform algorithm iterations are accelerating:</strong> The effective lifespan of the same creative has shortened from 7-10 days to 3-5 days</li>
<li><strong>User aesthetic fatigue is accelerating:</strong> Similar product creative patterns are quickly identified, increasing replication costs</li>
<li><strong>Test window competition is intensifying:</strong> The later entering the test phase, the more competitors your creatives face</li>
</ol>
<p>Simply put, <strong>the essence of cold launch is shifting from "testing a single product" to "testing a creative pool."</strong> The thickness of your creative pool directly impacts new product exposure quality during the critical first 7 days.</p>
<hr />
<h2>This Week's Recommendations: Minimum Viable Structure for Cold Launch Creative Pools</h2>
<p>Based on operational feedback from multiple projects this week, the following creative structure is recommended for new product cold launches:</p>
<h3>Basic Creative Pool (6-10 creatives)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Product feature showcase</strong> ×2: Highlighting core selling points, 15-30 seconds</li>
<li><strong>Use case demonstrations</strong> ×2: Showing authentic usage scenarios, enhancing immersion</li>
<li><strong>Pain point solutions</strong> ×1-2: Directly addressing target user pain points</li>
<li><strong>Comparison type</strong> ×1-2: Comparing with similar products or no-solution states</li>
<li><strong>User testimonials</strong> ×1: Prioritize authentic user content if available</li>
</ul>
<h3>Testing Rhythm Recommendations</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Day 1-2:</strong> All creatives tested simultaneously with small budgets, quick filtering</li>
<li><strong>Day 3-4:</strong> Preserve top 30% performers, scale up budgets</li>
<li><strong>Day 5-7:</strong> Add new angle creatives, maintain pool activity</li>
</ul>
<h3>This Week's Special Reminder</h3>
<p>"Native feel" matters more than "polished production." Mobile-shot content with subtitles often performs more stably than professionally produced pieces. Prioritize content authenticity during cold launch phases.</p>
<hr />
<h2>This Week's Summary</h2>
<p>TikTok Shop new product cold launch rules are changing: the speed of creative pool building and iteration efficiency have become core variables affecting cold launch success. It is recommended that teams review existing creative reserves this week, complete the minimum viable creative pool according to the above structure, and establish a 48-hour rapid testing mechanism.</p>
